    "description": "Position Project Manager Duty station Addis Ababa head office, with frequent project-site travel Reports to Chief Executive Officer / Project Director Employment Full-time, fixed-term project appointment Works with Project Officer, MEL Officer, Field Coordinator and cross-functional project teams 1.Project context Theday Agro Industry PLC is preparing to implement an inclusive fruit value-chain development project under the Mastercard Foundation Fund for Resilience and Prosperity (FRP). The project will strengthen direct sourcing from smallholder farmers, improve Good Agricultural Practices and post-harvest handling, support EU Organic certification readiness, expand regional distribution through youth-led enterprises, and develop local and export markets for value-added fruit products. It prioritizes dignified work and income opportunities for young women and men, including persons with disabilities and displaced young people. All activities and results will follow the final approved FRP work plan, budget and MEL framework. 2.Purpose of the position Lead end-to-end implementation of the FRP project, translating the approved business plan and contractual annexes into coordinated, accountable activities and measurable results. 3.Key duties and responsibilities Prepare and manage inception, annual, half-yearly, quarterly and monthly work plans, milestones, responsibilities and implementation calendars. Coordinate farmer sourcing, GAP and extension work, organic certification readiness, collection/logistics, youth enterprises, regional distribution and market development. Supervise assigned project personnel; organize review meetings, field follow-up, action trackers and timely escalation of implementation constraints. Coordinate with Finance on budget forecasting, eligible expenditure, procurement planning, coinvestment records and disbursement documentation, without replacing financial approval controls. Ensure donor agreement compliance concerning reporting, safeguards, procurement, consent and visibility, partner engagement, records and approval of changes. Lead consolidated progress reports, risk registers, corrective action plans and responses to donor monitoring, audits and independent verification. Work with the MEL Officer to review disaggregated Youth in Work outcomes, verify implementation records, prevent double counting and use learning to adapt delivery. Build productive relationships with farmers, government offices, training institutes, youth enterprises, distributors and technical service providers. Coordinate sustainability and post-project handover of farmer partnerships, enterprise-support models and market linkages. 4.Deliverables / performance expectations Approved inception and rolling work plans, milestones and activity tracker Timely narrative reports, risk register and corrective-action records Documented work-plan delivery and donor verification readiness Implementation close-out and sustainability handover",
